{
  "title": "108: Al-Kawsar الكوثر",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the name of Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful.\nإِنَّآ أَعْطَيْنَٰكَ ٱلْكَوْثَرَ (1)\nINNAA A-A’TAYNAAKAL KAWSAR. \nSurely We have given you Kausar,\nفَصَلِّ لِرَبِّكَ وَٱنْحَرْ (2)\nFASALLE LE-RABBEKA WAN-HAR. \nTherefore pray to your Lord and make a sacrifice.\nإِنَّ شَانِئَكَ هُوَ ٱلْأَبْتَرُ (3)\nINNA SHAANE-AKA HOWAL ABTAR.\nSurely your enemy is the one who shall be without posterity,",
  "merits": "There are 3 ayaat in this ‘Makki’ Surah. It is narrated from Imam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) that the person who recites this Surah in any of his prayers, will drink from the fountain of Kawsar. The reward for reciting this Surah is compared to ten times the number of cattle slaughtered on Eid-ul-Azhaa every year until the Day of Resurrection."
}
